  "detail": "Issue #377 was narrowed on 2026-10-14 (status comment on the issue): every invocation's descendants are already stopped before cleanup (#392), and `git clean` is already retried once and turned into round feedback. The one remaining gap is the gate-timeout re-run in src/pipeline/engine.ts (around line 1284), which calls `checkoutCommitted(cwd)` without the clean retry, so a still-running background writer there fails the run. This PR doesn't touch that path. Instead it adds a new invocation-level tracker (withInvocationProcesses in src/util/proc.ts, wired into RunContext.invoke in src/pipeline/context.ts) that aborts and awaits unawaited runProcess commands; nobody asked for it, it duplicates what #392 covers, and it rewrites runProcess, which another open PR (#624) is changing heavily. Remove the proc.ts and context.ts changes and their tests, and implement the narrowed fix: give the gate-timeout re-run's checkoutCommitted the same clean retry the initial gate checkout uses (`checkoutCommitted(cwd, undefined, Boolean(ctx.state.implementerIssue))` or the equivalent), with failure handled the same way as there. Add a test where the re-run's first `git clean` fails once (a writer still changing files) and the re-run proceeds, and one where it keeps failing and is handled like the initial checkout's failure. Keep to the issue's budget (a few source lines plus tests)."
 }
